! Silicon at a converged cutoff and a real k-grid, as the LDA control for TB09.
!
! QE's own two-atom cell (`test-suite/pw_scf/scf.in`) with three things changed,
! each of which the band gap needs and the SCF reference does not:
!
!   ecutwfc  12 -> 30    the gap is a difference of eigenvalues, not a total, and
!                        moves by more than 0.1 eV between the two
!   K_POINTS 2 -> 6x6x6  scf.in's two points are neither at Gamma nor near the
!                        conduction-band minimum along Delta, so no gap can be
!                        read off them at all
!   nbnd     -> 10       mBJ mixes the highest band of an `nbnd` window with the
!                        ones just outside it far more than a local potential
!                        does, so the window is opened past what is read
!
! There is no `pw.x` reference beside this one and none is possible for its
! partner `si2-tb09.in`: `pw.x` reaches TB09 only through libxc, passes a zero
! Laplacian and never sets `c`, so what it runs under that name is a different
! functional. This file exists so that the two runs differ by `input_dft` alone.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=2, celldm(1)=10.20, nat=2, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=30.0, nbnd=10
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-9
    electron_maxstep = 90
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 6 6 6 0 0 0
